BUGS

- infinite loop on invalid token out of scope (before LBRC but after other head token)
    -- reason is currently in parser_internals/parse.c, there is no check for validating expr_head,
       so, by default if no head patterns match, it falls through to parse_expr_stmt. 
       parse_expr_stmt actually returns a proper error but in jet_parse.c, 
       upon encountering the error, it tries to sync_toplevel which syncs back to the 
       start before the inv token and then same loop happens infinitely.
       
    * in parser_internals/parse.c/parse_toplevel dont fall thru to parse_expr_stmt, fist verify its a expression head
    * if all head checks fail, now call sync_toplevel inside parse_toplevel instead of inside parser_parse
    * crucially the head check should be more sophisticated, instead of checking only peek token, it should check for viable sequences.
      (basically check if recovery is possible by head pattern matching again before returning a valid sync point)

      e.g.
      ___________________

      type Vector2 #{..}
      ___________________

      Will keep repeat checking and failing up to invalid token <#> while calling sync when it encounteres <#>, will sync back to the keyword <type>.
      Thus repeating the failure cycle infinitely



